# Source files are text, and are to be diffed as text.
#
# git guesses binary-or-text by sniffing the first few kilobytes for a NUL
# byte. That guess was wrong here in a way that cost a review: a single
# literal NUL used as a join separator inside RecipientField.vue —
# `next.join('\0')`, a legitimate trick since no address can contain one —
# made git call the whole 13 kB component binary, so its diff rendered as
# "Bin 8550 -> 13670 bytes" and the largest file in a pull request could not
# be read at all.
#
# The NUL itself is now written as an escape rather than a raw byte, which is
# the real fix. This file is the guard against the next one: a control
# character that slips into a source file should show up as a strange line in
# a diff, not hide the diff.
*.vue    text diff
*.ts     text diff
*.js     text diff
*.go     text diff
*.sql    text diff
*.proto  text diff
*.md     text diff
*.yml    text diff
*.yaml   text diff
*.json   text diff
*.css    text diff
*.html   text diff

# Generated protobuf. Still text, but collapsed in review by default: it is
# regenerated by `make proto` and reviewing it line by line reviews the
# generator, not the change.
gen/**   linguist-generated=true
*.pb.go  linguist-generated=true
